## Dataset Management

### Dataset Lifecycle

```
┌──────────────┐
│   Created    │
└──────┬───────┘
       │
       ↓
┌──────────────┐
│   Active     │ (Used frequently)
└──────┬───────┘
       │
       ↓
┌──────────────┐
│   Warm       │ (Used occasionally)
└──────┬───────┘
       │
       ↓
┌──────────────┐
│   Cold       │ (Rarely used)
└──────┬───────┘
       │
       ↓
┌──────────────┐
│   Archived   │ (Compliance storage)
└──────┬───────┘
       │
       ↓
┌──────────────┐
│   Deleted    │ (Removed)
└──────────────┘
```

### Dataset Organization

#### Sequential Dataset (PS)

```
Record 1 ──► Record 2 ──► Record 3 ──► Record 4 ──► ...

Characteristics:
├─ Simple linear access
├─ Fast sequential reading
├─ Slow random access
└─ Good for batch processing
```

#### Partitioned Dataset (PDS)

```
PDS
├─ Member 1
├─ Member 2
├─ Member 3
└─ Member 4

Use Cases:
├─ Program libraries
├─ Job collections
├─ Data organization
└─ Team development
```

#### VSAM Dataset

```
VSAM Types:

KSDS (Keyed Sequential):
├─ Indexed by key
├─ Fast random access
└─ Used for database files

ESDS (Entry Sequenced):
├─ Access by position
├─ Preserves insertion order
└─ Used for logs

RRDS (Relative Record):
├─ Access by record number
├─ Direct access by position
└─ Used for arrays
```

### Dataset Management Tasks

```
Common Operations:
1. Create dataset with proper sizing
2. Monitor growth over time
3. Reorganize when fragmented
4. Archive when inactive
5. Delete when no longer needed
6. Backup before major changes
7. Verify integrity periodically
```

