## Performance & Optimization

### Performance Metrics

```
Key Metrics to Monitor:
├─ Disk I/O response time
│  └─ Target: < 50ms for random access
│
├─ Throughput
│  └─ Megabytes per second
│
├─ CPU utilization
│  └─ ICEMAN operations overhead
│
├─ Memory usage
│  └─ Cache and buffer pools
│
└─ Operation completion time
   └─ Reorganization, archival, etc.
```

### Optimization Strategies

#### 1. Disk Layout Optimization

```
Before Optimization:
Disk: [Data][Free][Data][Free][Data]
      Highly fragmented, slow access

After Optimization:
Disk: [Data][Data][Data][Data][Free]
      Sequential layout, fast access
```

#### 2. Caching Strategy

```
Cache Levels:
├─ Hot cache (Recently accessed data)
├─ Warm cache (Occasionally accessed)
└─ Cold storage (Rarely accessed)

Benefit:
├─ Faster access to hot data
├─ Lower latency for common operations
└─ Better overall system performance
```

#### 3. Compression

```
Compression Algorithms:
├─ RLE (Run Length Encoding)
│  └─ Best for repetitive data
│
├─ LZ4 (Lempel-Ziv)
│  └─ Fast compression
│
├─ Deflate
│  └─ Balanced performance
│
└─ ZSTD (Zstandard)
   └─ High compression ratio
```

#### 4. Tiered Storage

```
Tier 0: Flash storage (Hot)
        └─ Frequent access
        └─ Highest cost per GB

Tier 1: Fast DASD (Warm)
        └─ Regular access
        └─ Medium cost

Tier 2: Standard DASD (Cool)
        └─ Infrequent access
        └─ Lower cost

Tier 3: Archive/Tape (Cold)
        └─ Rare access
        └─ Lowest cost
```

