## Data Migration Scenarios

### Theory: Migration Strategies

```
Four Migration Approaches:

1. Big Bang Migration
   └─ All data moves at once
   └─ Downtime: 8-12 hours
   └─ Risk: High (single point of failure)
   └─ Use: Small systems, low-criticality

2. Phased Migration
   └─ Migrate by dataset/application
   └─ Downtime: Per-dataset (minimal)
   └─ Risk: Medium
   └─ Use: Medium systems

3. Parallel Migration
   └─ Old and new systems run together
   └─ Downtime: None
   └─ Risk: Low
   └─ Use: Critical systems, zero-downtime requirement

4. Rolling Migration
   └─ Migrate regions/segments sequentially
   └─ Downtime: None
   └─ Risk: Low
   └─ Use: Distributed systems
```

