## Performance Optimization

### Theory: I/O Performance

```
Storage I/O Stack:

Application Request
  ↓ (1ms - interpret)
Operating System (z/OS)
  ↓ (2ms - queue, schedule)
DASD Controller
  ↓ (3ms - process)
Disk Seek
  ↓ (5ms - head movement)
Data Transfer
  ↓ (10ms - read from platter)
Cache/Buffer
  ↓ (1ms - return to OS)
Application Response
  (Total: ~22ms for random I/O)

Sequential I/O:
  (0.5ms - no seek time)
  (Total: ~6ms for sequential)
```

### Optimization Techniques

#### 1. Defragmentation

```cobol
* BEFORE: Fragmented dataset
Disk Layout:
Block:  1    2    3    4    5    6    7    8
Data:  [A]  [X]  [A]  [Y]  [A]  [Z]  [A]  [FREE]
       ↑─────────────────────────↑
       Dataset scattered, slow access

* AFTER: Consolidated dataset
Block:  1    2    3    4    5    6    7    8
Data:  [A]  [A]  [A]  [A]  [FREE] [FREE] [FREE]
       ↑─────────↑
       Sequential, fast access

Performance Improvement:
├─ Sequential read: 3x faster (6ms vs 18ms)
├─ Random access: 10-50% faster
├─ Disk utilization: 20% better
└─ CPU usage: 15% reduction

ICEMAN Command:
EXEC ICEMAN REORGANIZE
    DATASET('CUSTOMER.FILE')
    RECLAIM-SPACE
    OPTIMIZE-IO
    RUN-WHEN(OFF-PEAK)
END-EXEC.
```

#### 2. Compression

```
Compression Benefits:

Scenario: 100GB database

Compression Algorithm Performance:

None:
├─ Storage: 100GB
├─ Read: 1000 MB/s (physical limit)
└─ CPU: Minimal

ZLIB (20% compression):
├─ Storage: 80GB (20GB saved)
├─ Read: 500 MB/s (time to decompress)
├─ CPU: 10% of I/O time
└─ Net: 20% storage saved, I/O limited

ZSTD (30% compression):
├─ Storage: 70GB (30GB saved)
├─ Read: 600 MB/s (faster decompression)
├─ CPU: 5% of I/O time
└─ Net: 30% storage saved, minimal I/O impact

Use Case Analysis:

Cold Data (Archives):
├─ Accessed rarely
├─ Maximize compression (ZLIB)
├─ Accept slower read time
└─ Save 30-40% storage

Hot Data (Active):
├─ Accessed frequently
├─ Use fast compression (ZSTD)
├─ Balance speed vs. storage
└─ Save 20-25% storage

ICEMAN Command:
EXEC ICEMAN COMPRESS
    DATASET('ARCHIVE.DATA')
    ALGORITHM(ZLIB)
    VERIFY-AFTER-COMPRESS
    STORE-METHOD('COMPRESSED')
END-EXEC.
```

#### 3. Caching Strategy

```
Three-Tier Cache:

┌──────────────────────┐
│  L1: Hot Data Cache  │
│  ├─ Size: 10GB       │
│  ├─ Access: < 1ms    │
│  └─ Cost: High       │
└──────────────────────┘
         ↓
┌──────────────────────┐
│ L2: Warm Data Cache  │
│ ├─ Size: 100GB       │
│ ├─ Access: 10-50ms   │
│ └─ Cost: Medium      │
└──────────────────────┘
         ↓
┌──────────────────────┐
│ L3: DASD Storage     │
│ ├─ Size: 1TB+        │
│ ├─ Access: 50-200ms  │
│ └─ Cost: Low         │
└──────────────────────┘

Smart Placement:

ICEMAN Tracks Access Patterns:
├─ Monitor all reads/writes
├─ Identify frequently accessed datasets
├─ Analyze temporal patterns
├─ Auto-migrate to appropriate tier

Automatic Promotion:
├─ Dataset accessed 10+ times daily
├─ Move from L3 → L2 (hot tier)
├─ Response time: 50ms → 15ms
└─ Worth the cost

Automatic Demotion:
├─ Dataset not accessed for 30 days
├─ Move from L2 → L3 (warm tier)
├─ Save storage cost
└─ Still accessible (slower)

ICEMAN Commands:
EXEC ICEMAN ANALYZE-PATTERNS
    DURATION(30-DAYS)
    TRACK-ACCESS(YES)
    GENERATE-RECOMMENDATIONS(YES)
END-EXEC.

EXEC ICEMAN AUTO-TIER
    RULE('ACCESS-COUNT > 10')
    ACTION('PROMOTE-TO-HOT')
END-EXEC.

EXEC ICEMAN AUTO-TIER
    RULE('DAYS-SINCE-ACCESS > 30')
    ACTION('DEMOTE-TO-WARM')
END-EXEC.
```

