## Troubleshooting Examples

### Issue 1: Dataset Corruption Detection and Recovery

```
Symptom: Application reporting data inconsistency

Investigation:
1. ICEMAN detects checksum mismatch
   └─ Dataset: CUSTOMER.MASTER
   └─ Records affected: 12,453 out of 500,000
   └─ Corruption date: Yesterday 14:30

2. Analyze impact
   └─ Customer IDs: 100001-112453
   └─ Data: Name, Address only (not critical)
   └─ Transactions: All valid

3. Recovery options
   └─ Option A: Restore from hourly backup
   └─ Option B: Restore from daily backup
   └─ Option C: Selective record recovery

4. Execute recovery
   EXEC ICEMAN RESTORE
       DATASET('CUSTOMER.MASTER')
       FROM-BACKUP('HOURLY-BACKUP')
       BACKUP-TIME('2024-12-31 14:00:00')
       VERIFY-AFTER-RESTORE
   END-EXEC.

5. Validation
   └─ Checksum verification: PASS
   └─ Record count: PASS
   └─ Data integrity: PASS
   └─ Application test: PASS

6. Root cause analysis
   └─ Cause: Disk read error (hardware)
   └─ Action: Replace disk
   └─ Monitoring: Enhanced error tracking
   └─ Prevention: Additional mirroring

Result:
└─ Full recovery, no data loss, no downtime
```

### Issue 2: Performance Degradation

```
Symptom: Database queries running 5x slower

Investigation:
1. Check fragmentation
   EXEC ICEMAN ANALYZE
       DATASET('ORDER.FILE')
       DETAIL(FRAGMENTATION)
   END-EXEC.
   Result: 65% fragmented (was 10% yesterday)

2. Identify cause
   └─ Large DELETE operation run last night
   └─ Deleted 1 million orders (order history cleanup)
   └─ Left gaps in dataset
   └─ Sequential reads jumping around disk

3. Check disk space
   └─ 30GB freed by deletions
   └─ Space scattered throughout dataset
   └─ Not consolidated

4. Recovery plan
   └─ Reorganize dataset
   └─ Consolidate free space
   └─ Rebuild indexes

5. Execute
   EXEC ICEMAN REORGANIZE
       DATASET('ORDER.FILE')
       RECLAIM-SPACE
       REBUILD-INDEXES
       PARALLEL-PROCESSING(YES)
       RUN-DURING-MAINTENANCE-WINDOW
   END-EXEC.

6. Verification
   EXEC ICEMAN ANALYZE
       DATASET('ORDER.FILE')
       COMPARE-WITH-BASELINE('FRAGMENTATION-BASELINE')
   END-EXEC.
   Result: Fragmentation reduced to 8%

7. Performance test
   └─ Query response time: 500ms (was 2500ms)
   └─ Performance restored to baseline
   └─ Scan efficiency: 90% improvement

Prevention:
├─ Schedule automatic defragmentation after large deletes
├─ Monitor fragmentation continuously
├─ Alert when fragmentation exceeds 30%
└─ Proactive maintenance before performance impact
```

